# Per-doc RAG eval data is generated locally and may contain customer content.
# The folder structure is intentionally committed (via this .gitignore) so
# `rag-testing/documents/` exists in fresh clones, but its contents stay local.
#
# Contents ignored:
#   <slug>/source.pdf        - the actual document (may contain customer data)
#   <slug>/metadata.json     - real upload_id / kb_id / org_id from the DB
#   <slug>/questions.json    - LLM-generated Q&A referencing the doc's text
#   <slug>/results/          - eval runs with retrieved chunks + generated answers
#
# To share a *specific* doc's eval dataset (e.g., a synthetic test KB), add an
# explicit whitelist rule below, for example:
#   !<slug>/
#   !<slug>/**

*
!.gitignore
